                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Easily the worst GameHouse original that I've played.  Game is super buggy, stutters, and seems to be missing some animations.  The story is a pretty weak but enough to convey the game from location to location.  Played the game on their hardest level and found myself finishing most levels with no issue and well before the end of each day.  \n\nAlso, I did notice0 an axed part of the game still was left in the finished product.  This isn't mentioned in the GameHouse walkthrough, but it appears most levels have a secret spot hidden in them... Not all the levels, but most.  If you click on it it says secret found and then does something.  In the first level a sombrero flips over, in another a bush creates bugs.  \n\nWhile I will finish the game to achievement hunt I recommend no one subject themselves to this one.  Play literally any other game from the Delicious/Blue Giraffe family of titles.",
